</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Statistics of the Sampled Testing Set</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the testing partition, we adopt a different sampling strategy from the training data, using a random sampling approach. The resulting sampled testing set preserves the same distributional properties as the original dataset.
Specifically, (1) the ratio of positive to negative instances remains consistent, (2) the distribution of relation labels is well aligned, and (3) the proportion of <span id="A1.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">no_relation</span> instances is maintained. These results confirm that our random sampling strategy produces a representative testing partition that faithfully reflects the characteristics of the original testing dataset.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T9" class="ltx_table">
